WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.020 --> 00:00:04.320
Good morning John. You just got back  to America from Jordan and Tunisia

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.520
where you visited refugee camps

00:00:06.520 --> 00:00:10.000
and I'm really looking forward to any Thoughts you might have from those Places

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:13.080
but in the meantime, here from my very safe location in Missoula, Montana,

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.660
I want to talk about the government of America.

00:00:16.660 --> 00:00:18.760
It's a mess, right? We've heard that it's a mess.

00:00:18.760 --> 00:00:20.740
I'm not talking about politics right now,

00:00:20.780 --> 00:00:22.660
Which is...I just don't want to talk about that.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:23.860
I'm talking about the federal government,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.360
that massive, inefficient bureaucracy

00:00:27.360 --> 00:00:30.240
that does Something, nobody really knows What,

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:32.920
We're spending a lot of money, nothing's getting done.

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:34.320
That, that's the idea,

00:00:34.320 --> 00:00:35.360
that we have in our heads.

00:00:35.360 --> 00:00:38.500
Well I'm going to take kind of a radical position in this video,

00:00:38.500 --> 00:00:41.360
And say that the federal government is effective,

00:00:41.660 --> 00:00:44.860
efficient, and surprisingly small.

00:00:44.860 --> 00:00:47.400
I recently asked my followers on Twitter some questions

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:49.540
about government employees.

00:00:49.540 --> 00:00:51.180
How many there are at the state level,

00:00:51.220 --> 00:00:52.340
the local level,

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:55.340
the federal level, military, education, that kind of thing.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:57.960
I asked those questions because I had looked this information up,

00:00:57.960 --> 00:01:00.920
And I found myself to be quite surprised by what I found.

00:01:00.920 --> 00:01:01.960
Pretty much everybody, including me,

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:03.840
thought that there were roughly the same number of

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.540
federal, and state, and local government employees.

00:01:06.640 --> 00:01:10.880
State and local governments employ more than 7 million people,

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:11.880
and that's not including education.

00:01:11.880 --> 00:01:15.560
The federal government employs less than 3 million people. Fewer.

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.400
People also dramatically overestimated the number of uniformed military we have,

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.540
and dramatically underestimated the number of people who work in public education.

00:01:23.540 --> 00:01:26.440
which is by far the largest category of government employee

00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:29.280
More than 7 million people work in public education.

00:01:29.280 --> 00:01:32.600
But here's the truly remarkable statistic that I couldn't even believe

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.820
when I first read it.

00:01:33.820 --> 00:01:37.560
Over the last 50 years, the number of federal government employees has increased

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:43.220
By less than zero percent. It has decreased.

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.180
It hasn't decreased a lot. But it has not gone up!

00:01:46.180 --> 00:01:49.160
So if the budget is increasing, the economy is growing,

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:52.920
the number of people in the country has increased by more than a hundred million,

00:01:52.920 --> 00:01:55.500
and the number of employees that manage

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.960
this government has not gone up, is it any wonder

00:01:57.960 --> 00:01:59.380
that it seems difficult

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:01.220
to deal with the federal government?

00:02:01.220 --> 00:02:05.060
There's more to manage and we're using the same number of people to manage it.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:09.040
Also the budget has increased dramatically, but the number of people we're paying hasn't.

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:09.900
What's going on?

00:02:09.900 --> 00:02:11.500
Well first, a lot of it is spent on contractors.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:15.180
so that's when the government gives money to a private company to do things for it,

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:17.500
Whether that's goods or services, it could be like a janitorial company,

00:02:17.500 --> 00:02:22.400
Just cleaning up office buildings, or it could be Lockheed Martin building fighter jets

00:02:22.400 --> 00:02:25.220
That all adds up to about 500 billion dollars

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:28.160
that's more than the federal government pays for its own employees,

00:02:28.160 --> 00:02:31.680
But still the budget is more than three trillion dollars.

00:02:31.680 --> 00:02:33.380
Where's all that money going?

00:02:33.620 --> 00:02:34.660
We give it away.

00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:37.640
64 percent of the money the government spent this year

00:02:37.640 --> 00:02:40.760
was spent on Social Security, Medicare, Medicaid,

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.940
poverty assistance, and veteran's benefits

00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:44.780
64 percent.

00:02:45.080 --> 00:02:48.380
If you take out all that stuff, state and local governments actually spend

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.800
significantly more than the federal government.

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:53.480
Politicians talk about skyrocketing spending,

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.140
and government bureaucratic inefficiency,

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:58.480
but those two things...have nothing to do with each other.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.020
Skyrocketing costs have far more to do with demographic trends,

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.680
and increases in healthcare costs

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.100
than they do with bureaucracy.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.720
So, if you're watching this, try to keep these things in your head:

00:03:09.720 --> 00:03:12.960
The number of government employees hasn't increased in the last 50 years,

00:03:12.960 --> 00:03:15.760
and those people do really good, important work,

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:17.060
and they're pretty good at it.

00:03:17.060 --> 00:03:20.460
State and local governments have a huge effect on the lives of the people living there,

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.420
and they actually employ far more people than the federal government,

00:03:23.420 --> 00:03:25.560
and those elections are extremely important.

00:03:25.560 --> 00:03:27.800
By far the largest category of government employee

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:29.020
is the Teacher,

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:31.800
and a significant majority of the money the federal government spends

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:34.040
is spent to help out old people,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:36.240
and sick people, and people who are very poor.

00:03:36.240 --> 00:03:39.900
and people who risked their lives to protect this country.

00:03:39.900 --> 00:03:41.560
John, I'll see you on Tuesday.

